    "body": "[PEP 751](https://peps.python.org/pep-0751/) allows extras and dependency groups to be selected when installing a lockfile. Existing pylock exports fix those selections at export time.\n\nAdd `uv export --format pylock.toml --multi-use` to retain selectable extras and dependency groups in the exported file, including their transitive dependencies. The project's selected dependency groups are included by default and can be adjusted with group flags. PEP 751 has no `default-extras` field, so extras must be selected at installation time; `--multi-use` cannot be combined with `--extra` or `--all-extras`. The existing `--all-extras` option keeps its single-use export behavior.\n\nMulti-use exports are limited to one project and reject declared conflicts, negative extra markers, group-specific Python requirements, and workspace-root dependencies or groups.\n\n<!-- codex-thread: 01a0f6df-5483-7713-880b-1d9b35a8669e -->",
    "closed_by": null,
