    "body": "### Summary\n\nI have a workspace project with several child members (defined via tools.uv.workspace.members = [\"shared/*\"].\n\nIn one of the child projects I have a tools.uv.package = true and a [package.scripts] section.  This project is also a dependency of the root workspace (to ensure it is installed\" on sync).\n\nhowever when I run uv sync it spits out a warning.\n\n```\nwarning: Skipping installation of entry points (`project.scripts`) for package `ccaas-data-tables` because this project is not packaged; to install entry points, set `tool.uv.package = true` or define a `build-system`\n```\n\neven though it actually builds the script in .venv/bin\n\nroot pyproject\n```toml\n[project]\nname = \"my-project\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nrequires-python = \"~=3.11.0\"\ndependencies = [\n    \"ccaas-data-tables\",\n]\n\n[tool.uv.workspace]\nmembers = [\"shared/*\"]\n\n[tool.uv.sources]\nccaas-data-tables = { workspace = true }\n\n```\n\nChild pyproject\n```toml\n[project]\nname = \"ccaas-data-tables\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndependencies = [\n    \"click~=8.5.0\",\n]\n\n[tools.uv]\npackage = true\n\n[project.scripts]\nmy_script = \"my_script:cli\"\n```\n\n### Platform\n\nmacOS 15.7.9 (Darwin 24.6.0 x86_64)\n\n### Version\n\nuv 0.12.3 (x86_64-apple-darwin)\n\n### Python version\n\nPython 3.11.13",
