    "body": "### Summary\n\nSimilar to #21846, running on NetBSD 11_STABLE. Seems to still be a problem.\n\n```\n-bash-5.3# uv --version\nuv 0.12.21 (x86_64-unknown-netbsd)\n```\n\nTriggers with Rust projects built with maturin. Specific packages: orjson, pyreqwest, ty. \n\n```\nResolved 35 packages in 5ms\n      Built pyreqwest==0.13.0\nerror: Failed to download and build `pyreqwest==0.13.0`\n  cause: The built wheel `pyreqwest-0.13.0-cp314-cp314-netbsd_11_0_STABLE_amd64.whl` is not compatible with the current Python 3.14 on NetBSD x86_64\n```\n\nLooking at the built resources for orjson, the actual built output seems to be fine:\n\n```\n-bash-5.3# cat orjson-3.12.0.dist-info/WHEEL\nWheel-Version: 1.0\nGenerator: maturin (1.15.0)\nRoot-Is-Purelib: false\nTag: cp314-cp314-netbsd_11_0_STABLE_amd64\n```\n\nImporting the library seems to also work fine:\n\n```\n-bash-5.3# file orjson.so\norjson.so: ELF 64-bit LSB shared object, x86-64, version 1 (SYSV), dynamically linked, for NetBSD 11.0, not stripped\n-bash-5.3# python3\nPython 3.14.7 (main, Sep 13 2026, 00:26:06) [GCC 12.5.0] on netbsd11\nType \"help\", \"copyright\", \"credits\" or \"license\" for more information.\n>>> import orjson\n>>> dir(orjson)\n['Fragment', 'JSONDecodeError', 'JSONEncodeError', 'OPT_APPEND_NEWLINE', 'OPT_INDENT_2', 'OPT_NAIVE_UTC', 'OPT_NON_STR_KEYS', 'OPT_OMIT_MICROSECONDS', 'OPT_PASSTHROUGH_DATACLASS', 'OPT_PASSTHROUGH_DATETIME', 'OPT_PASSTHROUGH_SUBCLASS', 'OPT_SERIALIZE_DATACLASS', 'OPT_SERIALIZE_NUMPY', 'OPT_SERIALIZE_UUID', 'OPT_SORT_KEYS', 'OPT_STRICT_INTEGER', 'OPT_UTC_Z', '__doc__', '__file__', '__loader__', '__name__', '__package__', '__spec__', '__version__', 'dumps', 'loads']\n>>>\n```\n\n\n### Platform\n\nNetBSD\n\n### Version\n\nuv 0.12.21\n\n### Python version\n\nPython 3.14.7",
