    "body": "## Summary\n\nWe record default groups and group Python requirements in `uv.lock` for workspace roots without a `[project]` table, making the root's group metadata available without rereading `pyproject.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[manifest]\nmembers = [\"member\"]\ndefault-groups = [\"docs\"]\n\n[manifest.dependency-groups]\ndocs = [{ name = \"sphinx\" }]\ntest = []\n\n[manifest.group-requires-python]\ntest = \">=3.13\"\n```\n\nWe keep root dependencies in `manifest.dependency-groups` and add Python requirements as a separate table that released readers can ignore. Empty groups remain recorded, and Python bounds include requirements inherited through `include-group`. As with workspace members, revision-5 lockfiles omit the implicit `[\"dev\"]` default; an absent default selection means `dev`.\n\nFrozen operations use the selected root groups' recorded bounds when choosing Python. Changing a group requirement or the recorded default selection makes the lockfile stale; lockfiles from before revision 5 remain usable with their workspace manifest.\n",
