    "body": "## Summary\n\nWe move workspace members' default groups and group Python requirements onto their package entries in `uv.lock`, alongside the groups they describe:\n\n```toml\n[[package]]\nname = \"member\"\nversion = \"1.0.0\"\nsource = { virtual = \"member\" }\ndefault-groups = [\"lint\"]\n\n[package.dev-dependencies]\nlint = [{ name = \"ruff\" }]\ntest = []\n\n[package.group-requires-python]\ntest = \">=3.13\"\n```\n\nWe keep the resolved dependency lists in `package.dev-dependencies` and record effective Python bounds, including those inherited through `include-group`, in the separate `group-requires-python` table. This also records bounds for empty groups, and released readers can ignore the added metadata.\n\nThis replaces the unshipped package-indexed `manifest.default-groups` and `manifest.group-metadata` tables. Packages with the implicit `[\"dev\"]` default omit `default-groups`, while explicit empty defaults and `\"all\"` remain distinct.\n",
