    "body": "We now respect dependency-group `requires-python` declarations at workspace roots without `[project]` when selecting and validating Python. For example, selecting a root group that requires Python 3.13 rejects `--python 3.12`, instead of accepting the interpreter and silently skipping the group's dependencies.\n\nThe selected groups' requirements include bounds inherited through `include-group`. Default groups participate in interpreter selection, and incompatible combinations identify the root groups contributing the conflicting requirements.\n",
