    "pull_request": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/pulls/22099",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22099",
      "diff_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22099.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22099.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "An x86-64 Python interpreter running under emulation on Windows ARM64 can report `ARM64` for `platform_machine` while its supported wheel tags contain `win_amd64`. When a lockfile is restricted to an ARM environment, the marker filter can infer that those wheels are unreachable and discard them. A later install with the emulated interpreter then builds from source unnecessarily, or fails if the package cannot be built locally.\n\nRetain `win_amd64` wheels when the dependency marker can describe Windows ARM. Explicit wheel-tag compatibility and `Requires-Python` checks still run first, so this does not make an incompatible wheel installable. This fixes existing emulated-interpreter behavior regardless of which Python architecture uv selects by default.\n\nPorts astral-sh/uv-dev#1384.\n",
    "closed_by": null,
