    "body": "### Summary\n\nAlthough `uv help audit` explicitly advertizes the flag `--no-default-groups` with \"Don't audit the default dependency groups\", passing this flag seems to have literally no effect. For instance, although `default-groups = [\"dev\"]` is specified in the `[tool.uv]` section of `pyproject.toml`, `uv audit` and `uv audit --no-default-groups` produce the same result (auditing *all* dependencies), whereas `uv audit --no-group dev` does successfully exclude the `dev` group.\n\nThis behavior is not only unexpected (as it's contrary to what happens, for instance, with `uv sync` and `uv export`), it also contradicts the documentation of `uv audit`.\n\n### Platform\n\nUbuntu 24.04 (WSL on Windows 11)\n\n### Version\n\nuv 0.12.19 (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu)\n\n### Python version\n\nPython 3.13.13",
