    "body": "## Summary\n\nWe make compatibility checking part of project Python discovery. `ProjectPythonRequest::find` returns the selected installation after reporting any incompatibility as a warning; `find_compatible` returns a `CompatibleProjectPython` or an error. Callers no longer validate a separately discovered interpreter.\n\n`PythonDiscovery` controls environment preferences, downloads, and interpreter reporting. We keep the requirement and its diagnostic sources in the request, and retain the selected installation together with its compatibility in a private `PythonSelection`. Only discovery can construct the compatible result.\n\nExisting environment reuse retains its own policy: `--no-sync` can reuse an incompatible cached environment, including when discovery must first locate its interpreter to find the cache entry. Interpreter reporting and compatibility diagnostics retain their ordering.\n\nAlternative to #22086, also stacked on #22018.\n",
