    "body": "## Summary\n\nWe introduce `CompatibleProjectPython`, which validates an interpreter against the resolved project requirement during construction. `ProjectInterpreter` requires this type for newly selected interpreters, and isolated `run` and `check` use the same validated discovery path.\n\nWe retain the contributing workspace declarations alongside the combined requirement, so validation and diagnostics use the same inputs. `uv venv` and `uv python find` continue to warn on incompatibility, and `--no-sync` can still preserve an incompatible existing environment.\n\nStacked on #22018. Follow-up to https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22015#discussion_r4137978367.\n",
    "closed_by": null,
