      "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22082.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds an `--inodes` flag to `uv cache size` to report the total number of filesystem entries (inodes) consumed by the uv cache rather than byte usage.\r\n\r\nThis is particularly helpful for users operating in shared HPC clusters and environments where strict inode quotas are enforced alongside disk capacity limits.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n- Added `--inodes` flag to `uv cache size`.\r\n- Implemented parallel directory walking via `ignore::WalkBuilder` for speed on large cache trees.\r\n- On Unix platforms, hardlinked files sharing `(dev, ino)` are deduplicated so they are not counted more than once.\r\n- Formats numbers with thousands separators in human-readable mode (e.g., `1,234,567`), while outputting raw integers in machine mode.\r\n- Added test coverage in `crates/uv/tests/build/cache_size.rs`.\r\n\r\nCloses #22053\r\n",
    "closed_by": null,
