      "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22080.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "We store shared URL prefixes once per cached Simple API response. Relative URLs share their complete base URL. Absolute URLs with paths share the literal scheme and authority (host, plus any port or credentials), while each file keeps its full path, query, and fragment as the suffix. Reconstructing a file preserves its original URL text and relative URL behavior.\n\nOn reads, we copy the archived prefix and suffix directly into the final URL. We avoid allocating temporary strings or vectors of decoded cache records. URL reconstruction retains the same allocation count as the parent PR: one for an absolute URL, two for a relative URL when the strings exceed inline capacity.\n\nArchived payload sizes for synthetic responses with 1,000 files:\n\n| URLs                |    Before |     After | Reduction |\n| ------------------- | --------: | --------: | --------: |\n| Relative            | 288,064 B | 192,160 B |     33.3% |\n| PyPI-style absolute | 288,064 B | 256,096 B |     11.1% |\n| Mixed               | 288,064 B | 224,192 B |     22.2% |\n\nSingle-file fixtures remain 352 bytes. These measure encoded size; runtime performance has not been benchmarked.\n",
