      "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22067.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "`uv build` can include a project's runtime lock in distributions. Under the `locked-tools` preview, it adds `pylock.toml` to the source distribution and wheel when `uv_build` is used and the project’s dependencies use PyPI sources. `tool.uv.export-lock` and `UV_EXPORT_LOCK` can enable export for other build backends or sources, or disable it.\n\nThe frontend checks workspace locks offline before packaging. When export is expected, a missing, stale, or unverifiable lock fails the build. Automatic export uses the lock to determine eligible sources, so a stale lock that still refers to non-PyPI sources can cause export to be skipped. Run `uv lock` before building, or explicitly enable export to require a lock. When rebuilding a wheel from a source distribution, uv checks its packaged lock and metadata before carrying the lock into the wheel. The packaged lock covers the project's runtime dependencies, rather than the full workspace lock. Dependencies on other workspace members and locks restricted to specific environments are not supported. The exported lock does not include optional extras or dependency groups; automatic export checks both for non-PyPI sources.\n\nFor `uv_build`, the frontend passes the formatted lock to the bundled fast path, which writes it during the build. The resulting wheel matches the PEP 517 path. Lock checks apply the build command's constraints and hash policy to any metadata builds.\n\nExport runs in `uv build`, including its PEP 517 path. Other frontends such as `python -m build` do not export the lock. The build backend does not need the lock exporter or its HTTP dependencies.\n\n<!-- codex-thread: 01a0d2d8-257a-7ab2-9b2d-04eb039f1ea9 -->\n\n",
