      "diff_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22063.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22063.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nWith `resolution-inputs`, omit fixed `exclude-newer` and `exclude-newer-package` values when the locked artifacts prove they are satisfied. Moving a cutoff earlier can then reuse the lock offline if every recorded artifact still predates it. Fresh resolutions, including `--upgrade`, use the current settings.\n\nOmission is limited to virtual projects and dependencies with wheels and no source distributions. Any sdist or buildable local/Git dependency keeps the cutoffs, since build dependencies can affect runtime metadata and are absent from the lock.\n\nRelative cutoffs, cutoffs for prereleases or missing upload timestamps, and package exceptions to stricter global or index cutoffs remain recorded. Validation checks the current effective cutoff, including index defaults, so removing an exception cannot reuse excluded artifacts. Preview-written locks also validate when the preview is disabled.\n\nWhen all global, package, and index cutoffs are absent or disabled, validation skips the package and artifact walk.\n",
    "closed_by": null,
