    "pull_request": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/pulls/22055",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22055",
      "diff_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22055.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22055.patch",
      "merged_at": "2026-09-28T20:43:19Z"
    },
    "body": "With `lock-without-metadata`, a conflicting dependency group containing both `requests<3` and `requests[socks]==2.32.3` can record a single resolved edge requesting `socks`. During lock validation, we retain the declarations' distinct version specifiers and incorrectly reconstruct an additional base edge, causing `uv lock --check --offline` to resolve again and fail with an empty cache.\n\nApply the existing extra-edge coverage check to declarations without extras too. Omit the separate base edge only when the locked extra edges cover its full environment. Collect the packages with locked extra edges once per group so unrelated requirements skip the coverage scan. Add regression coverage for different specifiers in an included group and for rejecting an extra edge that covers only part of the base requirement's platforms.\n\nCloses https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/issues/22046.\n",
    "closed_by": {
      "login": "charliermarsh",
      "id": 1309177,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDkxNzc=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1309177?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/charliermarsh",
