      "merged_at": "2026-09-28T21:21:44Z"
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds benchmarks for atomic writes and HTTP cache revalidation, to measure the ext4 behavior behind #22051.\n\nThe `atomic_write` benchmark compares `uv_fs::write_atomic_sync` and `uv_fs::write_atomic`. The `cached_client` benchmark calls `CachedClient::get_serde_with_retry` against a local server returning `304 Not Modified`, so it also measures the effect of switching the client to batched writes in #22056 and applying the filesystem fix in #22057.\n\nThe client benchmark revalidates 500 entries with 256 KiB payloads in one directory at concurrency 50. Fixture creation, flushing, and cleanup are outside the timer. It verifies that every request receives a 304 and rejects full response fetches. Both benchmarks run in the walltime job and remain available on all platforms.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Native and Windows Clippy passed for the new benchmark.\n- `cargo bench --locked --profile dev -p uv-bench --bench cached_client -- --test` passed on macOS; the instrumentation-mode skip also passed.\n- Rust formatting, workflow formatting, and diff checks passed.\n- Ran the same client benchmark across all three stack layers on a native Docker ext4 volume (Linux 7.0.12, aarch64, Rust 1.98.1, 8 CPUs). Criterion means per batch:\n\n| Implementation                   |     Time |\n| -------------------------------- | -------: |\n| Baseline in this PR              |  47.1 ms |\n| Batched writes (#22056)          | 568.5 ms |\n| Batched writes with fix (#22057) |  28.1 ms |\n\nTo run against a chosen filesystem:\n\n```sh\nTMPDIR=/path/on/ext4 cargo bench --locked --profile profiling -p uv-bench --bench cached_client\n```\n",
