    "body": "### Summary\n\nFor filesystems with inode quotas, it would be helpful to know how many inodes the uv cache is using, e.g.\n\n```console\n$ uv cache size --inodes\n12345\n```\n\nThis is particularly relevant to HPC clusters, which often have strict inode limits.\n\nTo implement this, I'm guessing the place to start would be an upstream PR into diskus to expose inode counts. I'd be happy to work on this, but first I wanted to see if uv would be interested in this functionality.\n\nIf the idea is acceptable, there are lots of little UI decisions to be made, for example:\n- Should the default (human readable) display use a suffix like 12.3K to match the byte counts?\n- Should the parameter be named `--inodes` or `--count` or ...?\n- Should the default display show size \\*and\\* count?\n\n\n### Example\n\n_No response_",
