    "body": "We now update the HTTP cache policy in place on a 304 response, avoiding a rewrite of the cached payload. The format change bumps the six cache buckets containing HTTP responses.\n\nWarm-cache benchmarks on Linux/ext4, with 96 entries and 16 concurrent requests per batch (`c9dab42be` → `1562e401b`, using SeaHash):\n\n| Warm-cache workload | Main | PR | Paired change |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 304 refresh, 256 KiB | 80.39 ms | 9.84 ms | 87.4% faster |\n| 304 refresh, 1 MiB | 323.20 ms | 17.59 ms | 94.6% faster |\n| Fresh reads, 4 KiB | 0.711 ms | 0.712 ms | Approximately unchanged |\n| Fresh reads, 256 KiB | 2.140 ms | 2.112 ms | 2.9% faster |\n| Fresh reads, 1 MiB | 7.529 ms | 7.698 ms | No clear difference |\n",
