    "body": "### Summary\n\nWith `lock-without-metadata`, `uv lock --check` always re-resolves when a group in `conflicts` lists a package with and without extras. Offline with an empty cache, it fails.\n\n**Edit:** #21951 partially fixed this, see below follow up comment. \n\nTurning the feature off, or dropping the conflict or either entry, avoids it.\n\n#### Why a project ends up like this\n\nWe lock two Airflow versions in one `uv.lock`, one conflicting group each, to test upgrades beside the current version. Each version's group includes a shared group with `apache-airflow`, then adds its pin with extras, e.g. `apache-airflow[celery]==3.3.2`. So one group has both `apache-airflow` and `apache-airflow[celery]`.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nRun `docker build . --progress plain --no-cache` on:\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM --platform=linux/amd64 ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.12.19-python3.12-trixie-slim\n\nCOPY <<EOF /mre/pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"mre\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.12\"\ndependencies = []\n\n[dependency-groups]\na = [\"requests\", \"requests[socks]\"]\nb = []\n\n[tool.uv]\npreview-features = [\"lock-without-metadata\"]\nconflicts = [[{ group = \"a\" }, { group = \"b\" }]]\nEOF\n\nWORKDIR /mre\nRUN uv lock\nRUN uv cache clean\nRUN uv lock --check --offline -v\n```\n\nThe last step fails:\n\n```\nDEBUG Resolving despite existing lockfile due to mismatched resolved dependencies for: `mre==0.1.0`\n  Requested: [Dependency { ... name: PackageName(\"requests\") ... extra: {} ... }, Dependency { ... name: PackageName(\"requests\") ... extra: {ExtraName(\"socks\")} ... }]\n  Existing: [Dependency { ... name: PackageName(\"requests\") ... extra: {ExtraName(\"socks\")} ... }]\n...\nerror: No solution found when resolving dependencies for split (included: mre[group:a]; excluded: mre[group:b])\n```\n\nWithout `preview-features` it passes: `Existing uv.lock satisfies workspace requirements`.\n\n### Platform\n\nLinux 6.1.29 x86_64 (AlmaLinux 9.2)\n\n### Version\n\nuv 0.12.19\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12.14",
