    "body": "## Summary\n\nWhen exporting a `pylock.toml` to another directory, `uv export` writes relative local paths relative to the project, but `uv pip sync` resolves them relative to the lockfile, as required by the [pylock.toml specification](https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/pylock-toml/#packages-directory-path).\n\nFor example:\n\n```sh\nuv export --output-file dist/pylock.toml\nuv pip sync --preview dist/pylock.toml\n```\n\nIf the project depends on `child/`, export writes `child` and sync looks for `dist/child`. Write `../child` instead. Apply the same rule to local archives and use the output directory when hashing them. For stdout, paths are relative to the current working directory, matching `uv pip compile`.\n",
