      "merged_at": "2026-09-28T16:00:47Z"
    },
    "body": "`uv python list` and `uv python upgrade` can panic when the managed Python directory contains an entry with an unrecognized implementation, such as `unknown-3.12.0-macos-aarch64-none`. Ignore these directories, as we do other malformed entries.\n\nInstallation keys also describe unmanaged interpreters, which can have unknown implementation names. Managed installations now store a known implementation, and both constructors reject unknown names. Looking up the implementation or creating a download request can therefore no longer panic on an unknown name.\n\n<!-- codex-thread: 01a0e706-a70b-7502-bc9d-2e500d9c1e1e -->\n",
    "closed_by": {
