      "diff_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22032.diff",
      "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/22032.patch",
      "merged_at": null
    },
    "body": "Closes #20908.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nWith `--no-build` (or `no-build = true`), a malformed PEP 508 requirement in `pyproject.toml` (e.g. a typo like `numpy<2.6>`) produced a misleading error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nerror: Failed to build `project`\r\n  cause: Building source distributions for `project` is disabled\r\n```\r\n\r\nInstead of reporting the actual typo, uv swallowed the parse error, fell through to a PEP 517 build to \"heal\" the metadata, and then failed only because the build was disallowed.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nIn `StaticMetadata::read` (`crates/uv-distribution/src/source/mod.rs`), when static metadata extraction fails with a PEP 508 parse error **and** a build would be refused for the source due to `--no-build`, surface the parse error directly (with source location) instead of falling through to the disallowed build.\r\n\r\nWhen builds are allowed, the existing fallback is fully preserved: the build backend still gets a chance to heal non-PEP-621-compliant metadata (e.g. Hatch's context formatting), so indirect dependencies keep working as documented.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- `lock::lock_no_build_invalid_dependency_virtual_project` now asserts the precise parse error with source span.\r\n- `pip_install::invalid_pyproject_toml_requirement_indirect` passes unchanged (fallback preserved when builds are enabled).\r\n- All 8 `no_build` lock tests and all 6 `lock_invalid*` lock tests pass.\r\n- `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy -p uv-distribution --all-targets` are clean.",
    "closed_by": null,
    "reactions": {
